=== HINT 1 ===
Map each type to the correct stdlib/math function:
  int    -> abs()
  long   -> labs()
  float  -> fabsf()
  double -> fabs()

=== HINT 2 ===
_Generic dispatch returns a function pointer or calls the function.
The cleanest form calls the function directly in each branch:

#define ABS(x) _Generic((x),   \
    int:    abs(x),            \
    long:   labs(x),           \
    float:  fabsf(x),          \
    double: fabs(x))

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
#define ABS(x) _Generic((x),  \
    int:    abs((int)(x)),    \
    long:   labs((long)(x)),  \
    float:  fabsf((float)(x)),\
    double: fabs((double)(x)))
